or risk-based authentication for a specific application in the tenant. See Create a New Rule.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-25\nValid as Of: 2024-04-25\nVersion: 26003\n\n--- Record 3034 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Social Identity Providers\nDescription: Twitter social identity provider was renamed to X in the administration console and the documentation of Cloud Identity Services.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-25\nValid as Of: 2024-04-25\nVersion: 26003\n\n--- Record 3035 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: User Tokens\nDescription: You can use the Maximum Exchange Period configuration in the admin console or the max_exchange_period parameter for the Token Endpoint for Resource Owner Password Credentials Flow to set а limit on how long the application can exchange user tokens without reauthenticating after having acquired the initial token. See Token Policy Configuration for Applications and Configure the Client to Call Identity Authentication Token Endpoint for Resource Owner Password Credentials Flow.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-25\nValid as Of: 2024-04-25\nVersion: 26003\n\n--- Record 3036 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Changing totalResults attribute calculation mechanism\nDescription: Identity Provisioning changed the mechanism for calculating the total count of users or groups returned by proxy systems when executing a SCIM Proxy endpoint request to read entities from a backend system.  As of now, if the backend system provides the actual value of the totalResults attribute and there is no condition defined in the read mapping transformation of the proxy system, this value will be returned in the response from the Identity Provisioning implementation of the Proxy System SCIM API.  Previously, the value of totalResults attribute was the sum of the request parameters startIndex and count. This calculation mechanism remains unchanged for backend systems which do not provide value for the totalResults attribute.  For more information, see: SAP Business Accelerator Hub: SAP Cloud Identity Services  Identity Provisioning Service  API Reference   Users/Groups\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-25\nValid as Of: 2024-04-25\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3037 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Renamed System\nDescription: The SAP Commissions connector has been renamed to SAP SuccessFactors Incentive Management.  For more information, see: SAP SuccessFactors Incentive Management.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-25\nValid as Of: 2024-04-25\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3038 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Apps\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Web & Mobile\nDescription:   Changed the default theme to SAP Morning Horizon for all new applications.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-25\nValid as Of: 2024-04-25\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3039 ---\nComponent: SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Support of new superdomain .cloud.sap for SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing applications\nDescription: You can use the new superdomain .cloud.sap to access the SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing applications for production and trial.  For more information, see Accessing the SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing Apps (production) and Accessing the SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing Apps (trial).  The previously known links are currently still working but not recommended for usage. A prompt switch to the new links is highly recommended.\nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2022-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-04-24\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3040 ---\nComponent: SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\n", "annel Promotion Pricing Apps (trial).  The previously known links are currently still working but not recommended for usage. A prompt switch to the new links is highly recommended.\nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2022-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-04-24\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3040 ---\nComponent: SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Enhance Search with Customer and Vendor Name for Business Units in Maintain Promotions App\nDescription: You can now search for business units Customer and Vendor using their names in the Maintain Promotions application.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2022-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-04-24\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 261 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Application Interface Framework Enablement\nDescription: You can build and manage your own application interfaces in ABAP development tools for Eclipse (ADT) with the SAP Application Interface Framework (AIF). Due to the lack of ADT for AIF, the development objects for asynchronous integrations (event consumption model and asynchronous SOAP services) currently generate their corresponding AIF interfaces with default monitoring settings automatically. With new AIF development capabilities in ADT, these AIF interfaces can be customized. Custom AIF interfaces can also be created, for monitoring the background processing framework (bgPF) in ABAP Cloud, for example.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-15\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 262 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Background Processing Framework - Final Version\nDescription: Background processing is very important for business applications. A lot of logic can be executed asynchronously to improve performance. In scenarios where changes of the current LUW are to be communicated remotely, the asynchronous execution is even mandatory to be compliant with the SAP LUW (due to implicit database commits).  We want to simplify and improve the background processing by covering all required qualities like: “exactly once”, “in order”, testability and an integration into the ADT cross trace for better supportability.  In the next step of bgPF the AIF integration and its monitoring capabilities are provided. In addition, \"in order\" capabilities are supported.  For more information, see Background Processing Framework.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-15\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 263 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Business User Authentication: Option for Configuring Secondary Signing Certificates\nDescription: Currently, only basic authentication is supported as authentication for SMTP outbound communication. With this feature, also the OAuth Client Credential Grant will be supported.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-15\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 264 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: CDS Hierarchy Generation Wizard\nDescription: Defining hierarchies for the use in a CDS view can become a complex task, with the need not only for the CDS hierarchy definition itself, but also for a directory, nodes, text views, and more. With the new hierarchy generation wizard, their creation becomes easier, quicker and less error-prone. The wizard will derive potential hierarchy nodes already from the start (on the master data view) and guide you through the creation process.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-15\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 265 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Change Document Reuse UI\nDescription: You can embed a reuse UI in your RAP OData V4 Fiori application.  For more information, see How to Use the Fiori Reuse Library.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-15\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 266 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Code Snippet in SOAP Service Consumption Model Changed\nDescription: The updated service consumption model improves the instantiation of consumer proxies and optimizes receiver determination through logical ports, enhancing SOAP service communication.  For more information, see Calling the SOAP Service.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-15\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 267 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Collaborative Draft\nDescription: You can now add collaborative capabilities to your business object. The collaborative draft allows multiple users to work concurrently on the same draft instance. See: Collaborative Draft Handling\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-15\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 268 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Cross-BO Transactional Enablement\nDescription: Cross-BO scenarios can now be transactionally enabled by defining a cross-BO context for the respective BDEFs. See:   RAP - Operations for Associations (ABAP Keyword Documentation)  RAP - with cross associations  RAP - AssocImplType\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-15\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 269 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Deprecated CDS Views in Business Event Logging\nDescription: The following CDS", "  RAP - with cross associations  RAP - AssocImplType\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-15\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 269 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Deprecated CDS Views in Business Event Logging\nDescription: The following CDS views have been deprecated:    C_BUSEVTLOGEVENTDEX_2 (Business Event Header Data (v2) ): Use the following successor: C_BUSEVTLOGEVENTDEX_3      C_BUEVLGEVTFULLPAYLOADJSONDEX (Business Event Data): Use the following successor: C_BUEVLGEVTFULLPYLDJSONDEX_2    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-15\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 270 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Expose Extensibility Status in Open Resource Discovery Document for Business Events\nDescription: The Open Resource Discovery document for business events now exposes the extensibility status.  For more information, see Outbound Event History.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-15\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n", "--- Record 3131 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Serverless module: Update to version 1.4.0\nDescription: With this update, we are introducing new versions of the Node.js (v20) and Python (v3.12) Serverless runtimes. At the same time, we deprecated the Node.js v18 and Python v3.9 runtimes. Migrate your Functions to the latest runtime versions. To learn how to do that, check the blog post Changing the function runtime version of a running function.  In addition, now the Serverless operator watches the number of Kubernetes worker nodes and uses smaller presets for the Function's build-time and runtime resources on smaller Kubernetes clusters.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-02\nValid as Of: 2024-04-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3132 ---\nComponent: SAP Build\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Manage Destinations – Enhancements and Updates\nDescription: In this release, we've changed enhance the destination experience:     The Business Application project type now supports destinations.      We've simplified the New Destination button and it is now called Add.      We have relocated the Delete option; it now appears under Actions. And we have renamed it to Remove for clarity.      To optimize usability, the Type and Host Address columns are no longer visible.      See Manage Destinations.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-16\nValid as Of: 2024-04-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3133 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Consume API Actions Using Integration Flow\nDescription: Your business processes can consume integration scenarios managed by your organization. To consume such integration flows, create an action project - using Integration Flow.  See:                  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-16\nValid as Of: 2024-04-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3134 ---\nComponent: Continuous Integration & Delivery\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Connections with SAP Business Application Studio\nDescription: The connection issue was resolved that prevented SAP Business Application Studio from connecting with the SAP Continuous Integration and Delivery service when performing setup with the booster.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-14\nValid as Of: 2024-04-15\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3135 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Upcoming upgrade to Kubernetes 1.28\nDescription: The Kyma environment is planned to be upgraded to the Kubernetes 1.28 version in the April 13th - 14th, 2024 maintenance window. For more information, see the Kubernetes release notes and the major changes in the blog post.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-29\nValid as Of: 2024-04-14\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3136 ---\nComponent: Availability Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Enhanced configuration option for Site24x7 monitors\nDescription: AvS now offers more configuration options and flexibility for Site24x7 monitors. For more information, see section Tester Specific Monitor Configurations in       Existing evaluations are not affected by the change.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-12\nValid as Of: 2024-04-12\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3137 ---\nComponent: Data Attribute Recommendation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Training Configuration\nDescription: The enableMasking parameter is now also available for the Sales Order Completion executables.  See Training Configuration.\nAction: Info only\nLi