ice Binding Validity\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-10-19\nValid as Of: 2023-10-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4035 ---\nComponent: Data Quality Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Enhancements\nDescription:     The microservice updated the country name for Turkey to Türkiye.      The microservice now supports address validation in Denmark to the secondary level. See Country Coverage for more information.      The address reference data for Argentina now includes postcodes in the 8-character alphanumeric format.      Improvements were made to the standardization of Israel addresses that are selected from type ahead suggestions.    The microservice now supports importing and exporting a country/region configuration in the Configuration Editor. See Rename a Configuration and Edit a Configuration for more information.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2023-10-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4036 ---\nComponent: SAP Alert Notification Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New SAP Credential Store events\nDescription: You can now use the newly supported Number Of Credentials Threshold Reached and Used Storage In MB Threshold Reached events.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-10-20\nValid as Of: 2023-10-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4037 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP Cockpit\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Enabling Horizon Theme in SAP BTP Cockpit\nDescription: The Horizon theme is now available in SAP BTP cockpit for SAP BTP, Neo environment and SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry environment. It introduces distinctive design elements aimed at helping you do your work faster, more intuitively and with better results.   The default theme is the light version of the Horizon theme, called Morning Horizon. The cockpit also supports a dark version called Evening Horizon as well as black-and-white high-contrast versions of the themes for accessibility to help people with visual impairments.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-10-19\nValid as Of: 2023-10-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4038 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP Cockpit\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Global URL\nDescription: Starting now, you can use the URL https://cockpit.btp.cloud.sap to access SAP BTP Cockpit (Feature Set B). Depending on your own geo location this URL will redirect you to the closest of the three regional Cockpit URLs (https://emea.cockpit.btp.cloud.sap, https://amer.cockpit.btp.cloud.sap, https://apac.cockpit.btp.cloud.sap).  You can also use deep links to get redirected directly to a specific page in the BTP Cockpit, for example, https://cockpit.btp.cloud.sap/cockpit#/globalaccount/<your-global-account>/accountModel.   Don’t worry - the regional Cockpit URLs we established recently, continue to work and we don’t plan to change that in the near future. The new global URL automatically chooses the best regional URL for", " https://apac.cockpit.btp.cloud.sap).  You can also use deep links to get redirected directly to a specific page in the BTP Cockpit, for example, https://cockpit.btp.cloud.sap/cockpit#/globalaccount/<your-global-account>/accountModel.   Don’t worry - the regional Cockpit URLs we established recently, continue to work and we don’t plan to change that in the near future. The new global URL automatically chooses the best regional URL for you.  Note that these changes only apply to Cloud Management Tools Feature Set B. If you want to learn more about the differences between Feature Set A and Feature Set B, check out our help page on Cloud Management Tools - Feature Set Overview.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLate